<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi bourse shut by strike by Moslem militants.</title>
<headline>Karachi bourse shut by strike by Moslem militants.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Karachi Stock Exchange closed on Tuesday because of a strike called by the militant Sunni Moslem Sipah-e-Sahaba Pakistan (SSP) group.</p>
<p>&quot;The bourse has been shut due to thin attendance,&quot; a spokesman for the exchange said.</p>
<p>The SSP called the strike to protest against the killing of its leader in a bomb blast in Lahore on Saturday.</p>
<p>On Monday, the Karachi 100-share index fell 8.19 points, or 0.57 percent, to end at 1,432.57 amid 101 losers and 76 gainers in a turnover of 24 million shares. -- Amir Zia 9221-5685192</p>
